 {flag}←{lineFlag}Pause msg;input;alias;ind;bool;NoPause
 ⍝ Prints `msg` to the session and tells the user that she must press `<enter>` if she wants to continue.
 ⍝ `msg` may be a simple character vector or a vector of them; `⎕UCS 13` is converted into `⎕UCS 10`.\\
 ⍝ By entering "`∘∘∘`" the user may interrupt `Pause`: this activates a stop.\\
 ⍝ The optional left argument `lineFlag` defaults to 0. If it's 1 then a line is printed. The length
 ⍝ is defined by `⎕PW-1`.\\
 ⍝ You can prevent `Pause` from displaying the message and requiring the user to press `<enter>`,
 ⍝ refer to the documentation with ]ADoc CommTools, catchword "Automation". Use "*" as ID in order
 ⍝ to suppress every call to `Pause`.\\
 ⍝ The function returns a shy result: 1 in case it did present the message and stopped, and 0
 ⍝ otherwise (when automation prevented that).
 lineFlag←{0=⎕NC ⍵:0 ⋄ ⍎⍵}'lineFlag'
 msg←⊃LF{⍺,⍺⍺,⍵}/⊆msg
 msg←ReplaceCRbyLF msg
 flag←1
 :If 0<⎕NC'∆Automation'
 :AndIf 0<≢∆Automation
     NoPause←(∆Automation[;1]≡¨⊂'Pause')⌿∆Automation[;2 3]
     :If AliasChar∊msg
         (alias msg)←SplitAlias msg
         :If 0=flag←~∨/(TakeAlias¨NoPause[;1])≡¨⊂alias
             'Pause'Log alias
         :EndIf
     :Else
         :If ∨/bool←NoPause[;1]≡¨⊂msg
             flag←0
             'Pause'Log msg
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
     :If flag
     :AndIf (⊂,'*')∊,¨NoPause[;1]
         flag←0
         'Pause'Log'*'
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
 :If flag
     :If lineFlag
         ⍞←((⎕PW-1)⍴'─'),LF
     :EndIf
     :If AliasChar∊msg
         ind←msg⍳AliasChar
     :AndIf ∧/~(ind↑msg)∊' ',LF
         msg←ind↓msg
     :EndIf
     'Pause'CallOnWait msg
     input←⍞,0/⍞←({0=≢⍵:⍵ ⋄ ⍵,LF}msg),'In order to continue press <enter> '
     :If '∘∘∘'≡¯3↑input
         (1+⊃⎕LC)⎕STOP⊃⎕SI
         ∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate stop caused by user input
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
⍝Done
